[{"id":"VRCE-5-61-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":1,"english":"And beholding that monkey place his crown at his feet the monkey-chief, with an anxious mind, accosted him, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"987eb4c199e726e5ae950322bab92a3811516589b078ff1d4f42856861d1962f","compact":"bc039dd28ea4c276aa9e4ddb0236342acdd0baaa607f8c917e84872dfe4ed4c5","nasal":"bc039dd28ea4c276aa9e4ddb0236342acdd0baaa607f8c917e84872dfe4ed4c5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":2,"english":"Rise up, rise up, why had you lain yourself at my feet? I declare you had you come here? It behove you to suggest the becoming procedure. Is it all well with my orchard Madhuvana? I long to know everything, O monkey.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.766,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c38bf5d4f7b0bb541b4cc486631155df6b1a501879cca0facb1af0197d14c804","compact":"b06ddb0b2271e23b74106a9683d85a70214ff77bc7eb25ccd7b7b990a8468e7e","nasal":"b06ddb0b2271e23b74106a9683d85a70214ff77bc7eb25ccd7b7b990a8468e7e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":3,"english":"Being thus addressed hopefully by the highsouled Sugrīva, Dadhimukha, gifted with an intelligence of a very high order, rose up and spoke.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"077a8fd880c344c028326923315bdfdfde4fce368c4274099732dd9991dc14d1","compact":"7aaf8cfe996b71af2455dd00c2aebc54745b644a4e78447b190c6aa726cd6ac6","nasal":"7aaf8cfe996b71af2455dd00c2aebc54745b644a4e78447b190c6aa726cd6ac6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":4,"english":"Neither yourself, nor Vāli, the lord of the monkeys, O king, allowed that orchard to be freely used by the monkeys but that has been now laid waste by them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.452,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"29b5e5a64a6f52d6932af66b7cd982291e807f152922c52f909f9e1049c60432","compact":"e2003fb7310be11ebf3f1518103708ef43a1d185f705ef09425efe0e87dc495b","nasal":"a93a18f3c6d0f86c377e3fec57317effc9ce5a830406ae3433c63fe04f805fcb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":5,"english":"I prevented them along with these attendants, but disregarding me, they drank and feasted there at their pleasure.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.197,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec1de48d903f1234a17a1fe921927a8c4b9c92ad7b5c055c211d0f83db9fa88c","compact":"939c87f878a729f3d0a5589c8136c3d4521403f91761786fb7827a129c613928","nasal":"0342dff2f98115c698693cc4eaba0fee1f87d186044897eacdf4a415f268bbf4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":6,"english":"Some of them went beyond the pale of food conduct, others ate at their pleasure, and all frowned (at us).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dc79c7bef5bcc159a2f0a810c1ff5bcb80bbd37ad189ec5503deb88ab517c53e","compact":"d82a76c416dbbfa75c6245a2a309783854af7929eb21c497a11213628774ed96","nasal":"259f55921e1c15944c71b2c643ff258188b21f44e1d10976eb9e730a1d6387df"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":7,"english":"When these attendants, being insulted by them, were greatly wroth, they were driven out of the garden, by those powerful and enraged monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.507,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd2ed09170d296d3eab9bb0bd963d42827e1cc0955b6673ad5f556c2527e3d26","compact":"e5855f766854da35ab3f9cc6516ea778c88009113fb87d1cb1cf7a05031ad64c","nasal":"bdb619f63b1904397c701046ecf9014c2bfa44c2ff22dd3e975208a2bfd17a05"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":8,"english":"They were greatly assailed by those many thousand heroic monkeys, worked up with ire and having reddened eyes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9e9766dfcd1c3af4626d8254d4710071802acadeac4fb1911548ab687eb97be2","compact":"ada772a40b8951143adae33995ab33aaa0c8ea662633adb146a4ffadfe6a0eaf","nasal":"ada772a40b8951143adae33995ab33aaa0c8ea662633adb146a4ffadfe6a0eaf"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":9,"english":"Some had their arins broken, some had their knee-joints crushed and some of them were thrown up in the sky.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9cd0d687d51d572bcd9414fdb95c218b034e33b7159b5f315c9c320fad0cf17f","compact":"77cb01731d92111ad207b923ed816fcff93e98b3f9385fc09d975a87f733140a","nasal":"77cb01731d92111ad207b923ed816fcff93e98b3f9385fc09d975a87f733140a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":10,"english":"Yourself their lord living, these heroes are beaten, and the entire Madhuvana is being freely enjoyed by them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f872a1d5d2cb437ccabb05e41a739b9d2bdc7359137b26694f3a0498edf358d7","compact":"0dd10a4614395185df4176914d6be484a40e22676eaa31439cfcd681c97492da","nasal":"0dd10a4614395185df4176914d6be484a40e22676eaa31439cfcd681c97492da"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":11,"english":"The highly intelligent Lakşmaņa, the slayer of foes, addressed Sugriva, the foremost O the monkeys, while he was thus being informed, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ffa38c56e317f2a73f66e8a6c80aeeda3c7f021c0e0a889878ae01010bdb0ad4","compact":"465466c4ba684ebd8e5920d9b439879171c7dd2c48743551658275bb34136e25","nasal":"465466c4ba684ebd8e5920d9b439879171c7dd2c48743551658275bb34136e25"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":12,"english":"O king, why has this monkey, the guard over the forest, come to you, and what sorrow has led him to give vent to these expressions?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a99052d365b311118a5ec1ffbd6553a9525d0830ad9a7afaf43ac78dbdc647d5","compact":"e190a398c210bfcb03129de3824cfba34b3da8648f64ee8e4f6c14b7d453ac1c","nasal":"e190a398c210bfcb03129de3824cfba34b3da8648f64ee8e4f6c14b7d453ac1c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":13,"english":"Being thus addressed by the high-souled Laksmana, Sugriva, skilled in the art of speech, replied.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"405a73f3ddd6845a466ec11260c6f2f556550cb750a91c946633eebdf6c440ae","compact":"ae864134bd1a7e256eafd10a100539cbe5b4e4b842b607c3cdb23cc82c39a6eb","nasal":"ae864134bd1a7e256eafd10a100539cbe5b4e4b842b607c3cdb23cc82c39a6eb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":14,"english":"O worshipful Lakşmaņa, the heroic monkey Dadhimukha speaks that the war-like monkeys headed by Angada have drunk honey.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b68ff14b2ee5b9e30f29af7bd526442a699dd6a5a0f141a189bff02eb3c30cb7","compact":"30eb48c378792f1fb0a9cbe46561405399cfa846ee2fe2e736777017212c375b","nasal":"af8237c91cf10042a520c2d11eccadcf88fbd72144c32771deb89b7f538b95f0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":15,"english":"If the monkeys had engaged in such an unfair proceeding without being successful in their mission, Angada would have looked poorly and his mind would have been overwhelmed with grief and forgetfulness.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.373,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-64-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"23720a5961a7b9a7f7a7a0ef05e002432760dce05428baba0283af78d2220924","compact":"ce71308b7b48c0d608eda643b33efc7c01f617bab254e6850c906daed0e3b829","nasal":"751004b756d7b561e99ac938c6cc4635934b49082b902e2b9d3d672d3a9c24a9"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":16,"english":"For this the warders were struck on their kneejoints for obstructing their revelry and for this they went so far as to disregard the powerful monkey Dadhimukha. I myself appointed this monkey the lord of my orchard. Forsooth has Hanumān espied the worshipful Sītā and none else. There is none else but Hanumān who is the instrumental of this work, for that best of monkeys has in him a high intellect, know the art of success, is gifted with courage, strength and prowess and is conversant with Śāstras.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.456,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-17","DUTT-5-63-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d9336f3eb3a56a8bcf12bf105242686c5665d992254216d0e61c249b6cdb1b22","compact":"15d7742a2b64d456844e1b4ac971afc5dc8895f43ab4d34ea5e9d76198d88d2e","nasal":"15d7742a2b64d456844e1b4ac971afc5dc8895f43ab4d34ea5e9d76198d88d2e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":17,"english":"There is none else but Hanumān who is the instrumental of this work, for that best of monkeys has in him a high intellect, know the art of success, is gifted with courage, strength and prowess and is conversant with Śāstras.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.692,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c6673359cfc8f4ab7bfa881f0722140b1d081b9857b4f001051655b4859dfc8","compact":"8e088951fdfdf78e732aca69450e2b2f04b492437e5bf29618e2dba6f4889f4a","nasal":"8e088951fdfdf78e732aca69450e2b2f04b492437e5bf29618e2dba6f4889f4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":18,"english":"No other wight is so qualified an instrument in encompassing this end. O you of excellent intellect, Hanumān know the art of success, is gifted with intellect, perseverance and courage and is versed in Šāstras. That work cannot fail, which is worked out by Jāmbavān and Angada and presided over by Hanumān.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.646,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-64-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"716a0df2cfd7b5e09f71243127e49083104b38673bd670d19573e8a4a8ae2288","compact":"8754c5537445047b9459f2113e28ef611961e935fdb6f47064c65175bc13751e","nasal":"82e6dda57ad04097ffeff186762392b6c8fefe02c75cf6594edf0f69936036cc"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":19,"english":"Forsooth that orchard has been laid waste by these heroes headed by Angada. And ransacking the southern quarter, those leading monkeys have come back and delightedly entered the Madhuvana. And the whole orchard has been explored and enjoyed by those monkeys and the attendants beaten and wounded on their kneejoints. To communicate to me this intelligence, this monkey of known prowess, and sweet accents, named Dhadimukha, has come here.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.629,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-20"],"status":"u