rs, the virtuous-souled Lakşmaņa along with Rāghava, was greatly pleased.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061024","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"772cc27d5eeb41efcb7ab3fdd3323a0563722fc07ea0c87e6de6ec678cd3cfc3","compact":"322c699924c87d2ed58864c5a8fa2b9c6793a67b62d3c84017d755be45c388f4","nasal":"322c699924c87d2ed58864c5a8fa2b9c6793a67b62d3c84017d755be45c388f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-25","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":25,"english":"Hearing these words from Sugrīva, pleasant to ears, the virtuous-souled Lakşmaņa along with Rāghava, was greatly pleased. And hearing this from Dadhimukha, Sugrīva, greatly gratified; addressed that lord of the for st, gain, Saying.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.495,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-23","DUTT-5-63-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061025","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ae83cc4fe013dd497a13d2ac5e232686f724903669073d42aabcbf85cf8b455e","compact":"4147938431a037dfec00876805fca88150cab07742446a3be2c11604faedecd9","nasal":"4147938431a037dfec00876805fca88150cab07742446a3be2c11604faedecd9"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-61-26","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":61,"verse":26,"english":"Greatly pleased I am, since, they, being successful, have explored this forest. And the insulting procedure of the successful is also pardonable. Do you soon go there and protect that orchards, and send here all those monkeys headed by Hanumān.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.721,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-63-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5061026","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5718820b41465102